{
  "title": "UX Design: From Research to Accessible Color Palettes",
  "description": "A practical introduction to user experience design for people who build web apps. You will learn the UX process (research, information architecture, wireframes, prototypes and usability testing), the visual fundamentals (hierarchy, type scales, spacing grids) and the laws of interaction, with their formulas. The longest chapter builds a complete color palette for a web app from first principles: the sRGB transfer function, HSL and why its lightness misleads, the perceptual OKLab and OKLCH spaces, WCAG contrast math, tonal scales placed by contrast, neutrals, semantic colors, design tokens, dark mode and color vision deficiencies. Sample JavaScript files implement every formula and generate a palette that checks its own contrast.",
